# Historical survey reference, NOT a SAR reconstruction
# Units: metres; axes x=east y=north z=up; separate simplified volumes
# Not georeferenced, not a watertight engineering model
# https://giza.fas.harvard.edu/pubdocs/131/full/
# 0 m = historical pit mouth. Pit-bottom and chamber-roof depths are distinct measurements.
# Simplification: The full shaft is drawn at its measured bottom section, 1.30 m east–west by 1.14 m north–south. The wider mouth (2.37 × 1.75 m), narrowing, turns, stairs and offering niche are omitted.
# Simplification: The rectangular room uses 2.72 m, the midpoint of the reported width range, and the measured 5.22 m southern extension. Its precise lateral offset is simplified.
# Simplification: The chamber floor at 27.45 m is derived from the observed roof at 25.50 m and measured height of 1.95 m. The 3 cm difference from the reported pit bottom is retained, not forced into agreement.
# Simplification: The report's conjectured original height of 3.16 m is not used. Masonry packing and contents are not modelled.
